Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Common/Math: complete the scalar CrossSIMD fallback

Two more members that only the no-SIMD branch of CrossSIMD.h lacks, found
the same way as the LoadF24x4 fix before it: by being the first build to
compile that branch.

  - Vec4F32::WithLane3From is implemented by the SSE, NEON and LSX
    branches and used by GPU/Common/SoftwareTransformCommon.cpp. The
    scalar Vec4F32 has WithLane3Zero and WithLane3One but not this one.
  - AnyCompareBitsSet(Vec4S32) is likewise implemented by all three
    vector branches and used by GPU/Common/DrawEngineCommon.cpp, and is
    missing from the scalar branch, which has only AllCompareBitsSet.

Both are written in the shape of the scalar code beside them rather than
translated from a vector branch. Compare masks in this header are all-ones
or all-zeros per lane, so testing lanes against 0xFFFFFFFF matches what
the movemask-based branches do.

diff --git a/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h b/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
index bab907de3..09ade151c 100644
--- a/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
+++ b/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
@@ -1801,6 +1801,10 @@ struct Vec4F32 {
 		return Vec4F32{ { v[0], v[1], v[2], 1.0f } };
 	}
 
+	Vec4F32 WithLane3From(Vec4F32 other) const {
+		return Vec4F32{ { v[0], v[1], v[2], other.v[3] } };
+	}
+
 	Vec4S32 CompareEq(Vec4F32 other) const {
 		Vec4S32 temp;
 		for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
@@ -1922,6 +1926,11 @@ inline bool AllCompareBitsSet(Vec4S32 value) {
 	return true;
 }
 
+inline bool AnyCompareBitsSet(Vec4S32 value) {
+	if (value.v[0] == 0xFFFFFFFF || value.v[1] == 0xFFFFFFFF || value.v[2] == 0xFFFFFFFF || value.v[3] == 0xFFFFFFFF) return true;
+	return false;
+}
+
 struct Vec4U16 {
 	uint16_t v[4];  // 64 bits.
 
